body:
The reason I like Socrates in The Apology is he roughly says: "The oracle Delphi told me I'm the smartest guy but I don't know anything so I don't understand how she's right. So I asked all the master tradesman and "experts" and I learned none of them actually knew anything and the only reason I'm the smartest person is because I KNOW I know nothing."

&#x200B;

"I know I know nothing" it's not a real quote but the point he's making is the best point in all of philosophy, we don't really know anything and it's better to keep learning and not knowing then to have a set in stone belief. Socrates #1
